  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">My Village (MVi) was founded in November 2006 and officially registered with the Ministry of Interior in 25 January 2007. Ever since, MVi became a recognized local NGO working for Indigenous Peoples&apos; Rights and Natural Resources Management. MVi encourages ownership and participation of Indigenous Peoples# as its approaches to protect their land and natural resources.
MVi is operating in Northeast provinces of Cambodia, in particular in Mondulkiri, Kratie and Stung Treng, and focused on organizing community forests, helping indigenous people learn about their rights, helping women become empowered, and facilitating communities in undertaking various development projects.
MVi has been worked in collaboration with Community Networks, Provincial and National NGO networks, and line of government institutions at the national and provincial level of Department of Local Administrative of Ministry of Interior, Department of Forestry Administrative, Department of Agriculture, Department of Environment, Department of Land Use Management, and Department of Rural Development.</narrative>
  </description>
